  "header": {
    "format_version": 0,
    "format_revision": 1,
    "case_name": "IEEE13",
    "case_description": "Full IEEE 13-node feeder graph projected onto the currently implemented fixed-ABC EMT model subset",
    "case_comments": "This is explicitly not an exact IEEE 13-node benchmark model. It retains every feeder bus and branch in the published 650-632-670-671 topology that can be connected with the available components. The 650 regulator and RG60 internal node are contracted into the source connection; the 115/4.16-kV substation transformer ratio is collapsed into a 4.16-kV source with its published 1-percent R and 8-percent X series impedance; the 633-634 4.16/0.48-kV transformer is a unity-ratio three-phase series LineLumped proxy with a 1-percent symmetric mutual completion and loads referred to 4.16 kV. Because the fixed-ABC Bus contract makes all bus voltages differential, that proxy uses a full-rank shunt-capacitance regularization equal to the adjacent 632-633 segment's total capacitance; it is not sourced IEEE transformer capacitance. Configurations 603 and 604 repeat the mean published two-phase self term and published mutual term across ABC; 605 scales those 603 mutual-to-self ratios to its published scalar self data; 607 scales the full 606 coupling pattern to its published scalar self data. The closed 671-692 switch is represented by a one-metre configuration-601 LineLumped jumper. Constant-P and constant-I loads and delta connections are replaced by nominal-voltage grounded-wye RL equivalents; unloaded projected phases use finite open-circuit impedances; capacitors at 675 and 611 are omitted because no supported component can represent them. There are no regulator taps, transformer ratio, capacitor, phase-selective, PQ, or constant-current dynamics. Published IEEE PES topology/load data and current EPRI OpenDSS line matrices are used where the fixed-ABC lane can represent them.",
    "omega0": 376.99111843077515
  },
